{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel5 \b \fs16 Effects of Withdrawal\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If you withdraw from this contract, we shall reimburse to you all payments received from you without undue delay and in any event not later than 14 days from the day on which we are informed about your decision to withdraw from this contract. We will carry out such reimbursement using the same means of payment as you used for the initial transaction, unless you have expressly agreed otherwise; in any event, you will not incur any fees as a result of such reimbursement.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 If you requested to begin the performance of services during the withdrawal period, you shall pay us an amount which is in proportion to what has been provided until you have communicated to us your withdrawal from this contract, in comparison with the full coverage of the contract.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 \outlinelevel5 \b \fs16 Expiry of the Right of Withdrawal\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 (a) Digital content not supplied on a physical medium (Part A, e.g. the dBdone App, plugins and Credits): Your right of withdrawal expires prematurely (\u167 ? 356 (5) BGB) once we have begun to perform the contract, after you (1) have expressly consented that we begin performance before the end of the withdrawal period, (2) have acknowledged that by giving this consent you lose your right of withdrawal once performance has begun, and (3) we have provided you with a confirmation of the contract including these declarations by e-mail. At the checkout, you give this consent and acknowledgement by confirming the statement "I agree to the Terms and request immediate access to the digital content. I understand that I lose my right of withdrawal once it has been provided."; the purchase confirmation e-mail repeats it.\par}
{\pard \ql \f0 \sa180 \li0 \fi0 (b) Subscriptions and online services (Part B, e.g. Spaces and the Bedroom and Studio bundles): If you have requested that the service starts during the withdrawal period (at the checkout: "I agree to the Terms and request that the service starts immediately."), you keep your right of withdrawal, but in the event of withdrawal you shall pay us a proportionate amount for the service provided until you inform us of the withdrawal (\u167 ? 357a (2) BGB). The right of withdrawal expires prematurely only if the service has been completely performed and you have expressly consented to the start of performance before the end of the withdrawal period and acknowledged that you lose your right of withdrawal upon complete performance of the contract (\u167 ? 356 (4) BGB).\par}
